<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS GASOLINE PRICES BY ONE CENT.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS GASOLINE PRICES BY ONE CENT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Monday it will cut its retail prices for gasolines in the Netherlands by one cent per litre with effect from October 30.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said, adding the diesel prices remained unchanged.</p>
<p>From Wednesday the price of premium unleaded gasoline at Shell's self-service stations falls to 2.09 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>The price of premium with lead substitute falls to 2.15 guilders and that of Euro regular unleaded to 2.04 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
